classical inverse probability of treatment weights (IPTW). Other methods
(e.g. \code{"ebal"}, \code{"cbps"}, \code{"energy"}) and estimands (e.g. \code{"ATT"}, \code{"ATC"},
\code{"ATO"}) can be selected via \code{method} and \code{estimand}; which combinations are
valid depends on \pkg{WeightIt} and on the number of treatment levels.
Additional arguments (e.g. \code{link}, \code{missing}) are passed on through \code{...}.

The number of treatment levels is detected automatically:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Two levels:} if the chosen method estimates a propensity score (e.g.
